    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1046">

                <pb facs="0942" n="838" sameAs="frus:frus1913/pg838"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.00/9181.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The American Chargé
                            d’Affaires to the Secretary of
                        State.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram—Paraphrase.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Embassy</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Mexico</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1913-10-13T10:00:00-06:36">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">October 13, 1913—10 a.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>548. Department’s October 12, midnight. General Huerta last night said that no
                    violence whatsoever would be done to the deputies but that they must in many
                    cases stand trial for sedition and treason. He requested me to assure my
                    Government that they would be tried fairly by the civil courts.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Nelson O’Shaughnessy</hi>.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
